1
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:47,970
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:51,080
[Episode 1]

3
00:01:57,380 --> 00:01:58,780
[Domestic Security Check]

4
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,209
Sorry, the subscriber

5
00:02:05,210 --> 00:02:06,369
you dialed

6
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:08,370
cannot be connected for the moment.

7
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:10,410
Miss. Miss.

8
00:02:10,710 --> 00:02:12,239
We're just one person short.

9
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,556
We'll get there right on time.
No, thanks.
We'll be there in 20 minutes, I promise.

10
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:14,580
No, thank you.
Miss,

11
00:02:14,910 --> 00:02:15,690
you're from out of town, right?

12
00:02:15,691 --> 00:02:16,899
I see you've been standing there for ages.

13
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:17,976
Don't have a place to stay?
Come stay at our inn.

14
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:18,590
No need, someone's picking me up.

15
00:02:18,591 --> 00:02:19,619
Our inn is just nearby.

16
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:20,626
I'm not here for traveling.
Miss.

17
00:02:20,650 --> 00:02:22,036
It's cheap and clean.
We got all good reviews.

18
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:23,460
I'll give you a discount!

19
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:26,859
It's been an hour.

20
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:28,790
Why isn't she answering the phone?

21
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:31,000
Miss He.
I've been at the airport

22
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:32,150
for an hour now,

23
00:02:32,151 --> 00:02:33,589
but I haven't been able to reach you.

24
00:02:33,590 --> 00:02:34,809
I'm not sure what's going on.

25
00:02:34,810 --> 00:02:35,839
It's getting late.

26
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,529
Please send someone to pick
me up as soon as possible.

27
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:38,530
Thank you.

28
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,710
Does it sound a bit too harsh?

29
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:49,470
Hello, Miss He.

30
00:02:49,579 --> 00:02:50,310
Sorry to bother you.

31
00:02:50,311 --> 00:02:51,410
May I ask...

32
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,240
You...

33
00:02:56,030 --> 00:02:56,430
Hi.

34
00:02:56,810 --> 00:02:58,210
Excuse me.
Are you here on vacation?

35
00:02:58,410 --> 00:02:58,800
No need.

36
00:02:58,801 --> 00:03:00,330
I'm not looking for a hotel.

37
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,360
No, no. I just wanted

38
00:03:01,361 --> 00:03:03,120
to add you on WeChat.

39
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:04,860
Don't worry,

40
00:03:04,861 --> 00:03:05,899
I'm not a bad person,

41
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:08,089
and I'm not trying to lure you
into staying at my hotel or anything.

42
00:03:08,090 --> 00:03:09,950
I just want to be friends with you.

43
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,409
You're a student, right?

44
00:03:12,410 --> 00:03:13,470
I'm a student, too.

45
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:16,360
Don't believe me?

46
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:17,496
I can show you my student ID.

47
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:18,619
No, no. No need.

48
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:19,620
No need.

49
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:21,190
Then,

50
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,680
let me add you on WeChat first.
I'll scan you.

51
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:24,810
Come on.

52
00:03:28,650 --> 00:03:29,650
Accept it.

53
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:38,590
Steal A Moment... To
Sip Wine... Guesthouse?

54
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,140
That's not important.

55
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:42,530
Are you going to EAW?

56
00:03:44,710 --> 00:03:45,810
How do you know?

57
00:03:47,030 --> 00:03:47,620
Sorry.

58
00:03:47,621 --> 00:03:49,469
When I was adding you,

59
00:03:49,470 --> 00:03:50,529
I accidentally saw it.

60
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:51,530
I didn't mean it.

61
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:54,340
Well,

62
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,280
aren't you here a bit too early?

63
00:03:57,190 --> 00:03:57,900
EAW

64
00:03:57,901 --> 00:03:59,679
won't open until the end of the month.

65
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,910
I was invited here.

66
00:04:01,410 --> 00:04:02,410
Invited?

67
00:04:02,810 --> 00:04:03,150
So you're

68
00:04:03,151 --> 00:04:04,519
one of the invited content creators, right?

69
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,520
Yes.

70
00:04:06,750 --> 00:04:08,680
Come with me. It's on my way anyway.

71
00:04:10,410 --> 00:04:11,470
Speaking of which,

72
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:12,860
EAW

73
00:04:13,410 --> 00:04:15,470
actually has something to do with me.

74
00:04:15,810 --> 00:04:16,810
EAW...

75
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:18,240
My brother owns it.

76
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:20,540
What is he trying to do?

77
00:04:21,070 --> 00:04:23,219
Why doesn't he just brag
that he owns it himself?

78
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:24,480
It's too much trouble.

79
00:04:24,510 --> 00:04:25,559
I'll go...

80
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,080
I'll go that way.
I... I'm leaving now.

81
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:28,180
Bye-bye.

82
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:29,890
It's really no trouble.

83
00:04:35,370 --> 00:04:36,370
Sure, sure.

84
00:04:40,570 --> 00:04:41,629
Hello, Miss He.

85
00:04:41,630 --> 00:04:43,099
Ms. Idle Cloud, I'm so sorry.

86
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:44,599
I accidentally fell asleep

87
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,929
and didn't notice that
the driver had canceled

88
00:04:45,930 --> 00:04:47,099
my airport pickup at the last minute.

89
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:47,870
I-It's okay.

90
00:04:47,871 --> 00:04:50,540
I... I only just arrived not long ago.

91
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:52,039
I've already contacted someone else

92
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:52,950
to come pick you up.

93
00:04:52,951 --> 00:04:54,539
I've sent the license
plate number to your phone.

94
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:55,540
I-It's alright.

95
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:57,629
See you tomorrow.

96
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:58,630
Okay, bye-bye.

97
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:08,170
That must've been the driver calling.

98
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:16,830
Hello?

99
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:18,570
Sorry.

100
00:05:18,571 --> 00:05:19,900
I accidentally hung up.

101
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:20,680
Are you

102
00:05:20,681 --> 00:05:21,830
from EAW?

103
00:05:22,830 --> 00:05:24,360
Come out, cross the street,

104
00:05:25,270 --> 00:05:26,870
and you'll see a parking lot.

105
00:05:27,750 --> 00:05:28,630
I... Alright, I'll

106
00:05:28,631 --> 00:05:30,030
come out and find you now.

107
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:31,679
Did you bring an umbrella?

108
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:32,680
I did.

109
00:05:33,310 --> 00:05:35,279
I'll wait for you in the parking lot.

110
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:35,820
Okay.

111
00:05:35,850 --> 00:05:36,980
I'll be right there.

112
00:06:14,510 --> 00:06:15,510
Hello.
Are you the driver

113
00:06:16,010 --> 00:06:17,010
from EAW?

114
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,939
Could you open the trunk, please?

115
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:20,940
Thank you.

116
00:06:43,790 --> 00:06:45,390
It's okay. I can do it myself.

117
00:06:45,890 --> 00:06:47,120
Thank you.

118
00:06:55,130 --> 00:06:56,130
No need.

119
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,580
There are tissues down there.

120
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:32,860
Thank you.

121
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:42,270
S-Sorry

122
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,060
for troubling you

123
00:07:43,061 --> 00:07:44,920
to come pick me up so late at night.

124
00:07:47,950 --> 00:07:48,950
Where to?

125
00:07:50,690 --> 00:07:51,860
Yangjin Hotel.

126
00:07:51,950 --> 00:07:52,950
Thank you.

127
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,720
About how long will it take?

128
00:08:17,130 --> 00:08:18,130
30 minutes.

129
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:21,060
Okay.

130
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,460
Why are we taking such a remote route?

131
00:08:43,679 --> 00:08:45,909
I've already transferred the money to you.

132
00:08:45,910 --> 00:08:46,910
Cut the crap.

133
00:08:47,150 --> 00:08:48,150
Money?
What money?

134
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:51,750
I hope he hasn't sold me already.

135
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,980
Why is he looking at me?

136
00:09:07,550 --> 00:09:08,390
Help.

137
00:09:08,391 --> 00:09:09,940
Where is this?

138
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:16,580
The highway is under repair.

139
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:18,060
This route is faster.

140
00:09:19,890 --> 00:09:21,150
I... I'm not in a hurry.

141
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:22,500
Not at all.

142
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,360
Thank you.

143
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:53,860
I can do it myself.

144
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,320
W-Wait a minute.

145
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:12,179
The rain probably won't stop any time soon.

146
00:10:12,180 --> 00:10:13,460
I'll be stopping by
EAW tomorrow.

147
00:10:14,130 --> 00:10:16,260
You can just leave it at the front desk.

148
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:30,119
We've arrived at Xifu
Experimental Middle School.

149
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:31,289
Passengers getting off,

150
00:11:31,290 --> 00:11:33,220
please exit through the rear door.

151
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,200
Dear.

152
00:13:09,550 --> 00:13:12,080
Why are you picking a
fight with our daughter?

153
00:13:12,170 --> 00:13:14,170
How is this picking a fight with her?

154
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,720
I'm just looking out for her.

155
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:17,740
Yun Ye.

156
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:22,810
Did she pick up the phone?

157
00:13:23,410 --> 00:13:24,410
No.

158
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,600
Keep calling until she does.

159
00:13:29,010 --> 00:13:30,010
Do it right here!

160
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:31,670
I'll watch you!

161
00:13:43,630 --> 00:13:44,630
She hung up.

162
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:02,099
I already made it clear.

163
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:03,579
Why are you calling me again?

164
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:04,900
Hello, Li? Li,
hurry and tell Dad.

165
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:05,870
T-Tell him

166
00:14:05,871 --> 00:14:06,959
that we weren't in on this together.

167
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,420
Hurry up a-and tell him...

168
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:11,720
Where are you?

169
00:14:11,750 --> 00:14:13,369
You think you're all grown up now, huh?

170
00:14:13,370 --> 00:14:15,169
I just scolded you a little,
and now you're not coming home?

171
00:14:15,170 --> 00:14:16,230
I'm in Nanwu.

172
00:14:16,270 --> 00:14:17,800
What are you doing in Nanwu?

173
00:14:18,670 --> 00:14:20,410
I'm attending an event

174
00:14:21,290 --> 00:14:22,839
and getting to know the
campus while I'm there.

175
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:24,319
I won't be coming back for now.

176
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:25,120
And I'm going to look for

177
00:14:25,121 --> 00:14:26,819
an internship here afterward.

178
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:27,820
No, you're not!

179
00:14:27,870 --> 00:14:29,659
Why did you have to go so far away?

180
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:30,170
Come back

181
00:14:30,171 --> 00:14:31,239
and just stay at home.

182
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:32,560
Either find yourself a job
in Xifu

183
00:14:33,010 --> 00:14:33,980
or reapply for

184
00:14:33,981 --> 00:14:35,710
a local graduate program here.

185
00:14:37,670 --> 00:14:39,770
D-Don't be so bossy.

186
00:14:39,790 --> 00:14:42,120
At least listen to
what Li has to say first.

187
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:44,110
Dad, you don't understand.

188
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:45,739
NUST is a great university.

189
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:46,170
Its automation program

190
00:14:46,171 --> 00:14:47,769
is one of the best in the country.

191
00:14:47,770 --> 00:14:48,670
Stop talking about that.

192
00:14:48,671 --> 00:14:50,319
Book a flight and come back right away.

193
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:51,320
I won't!

194
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,080
Lili,

195
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:57,599
your dad is only saying this
because he cares about you.

196
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:58,550
This is the first time

197
00:14:58,551 --> 00:15:01,119
you've gone somewhere
so far away by yourself.

198
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:02,780
We're just worried about you.

199
00:15:03,010 --> 00:15:04,859
If you have any plans

200
00:15:04,860 --> 00:15:06,149
for your studies or career,

201
00:15:06,150 --> 00:15:08,080
just talk them through with Dad.

202
00:15:08,910 --> 00:15:10,640
There's nothing to talk about.

203
00:15:10,670 --> 00:15:11,859
Either come back now,

204
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:13,250
or don't ever come back.

205
00:15:13,450 --> 00:15:15,839
Don't even think about
taking a single penny from us.

206
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:17,479
Wait. I'm just doing my internship

207
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:18,619
and looking for a job in another city.

208
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:20,259
What's the problem with that?

209
00:15:20,260 --> 00:15:20,860
It's not like

210
00:15:20,861 --> 00:15:22,550
I'm never coming back.

211
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:24,859
Every time I try to have a
proper conversation with you,

212
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:26,959
when have you ever actually listened?

213
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,269
I can't even finish a sentence

214
00:15:28,270 --> 00:15:29,956
before you shut me down.
Other than disagreeing with me,

215
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:31,380
what else do you ever say?

216
00:15:31,550 --> 00:15:32,550
Lili.

217
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:34,250
Lili.

218
00:15:34,251 --> 00:15:35,850
Don't take it out on your dad.

219
00:15:36,250 --> 00:15:38,410
You know what he's like.

220
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:42,050
He's harsh on the outside
but soft on the inside.

221
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,980
Talk some sense into your sister.

222
00:15:45,410 --> 00:15:46,250
Li. Li,

223
00:15:46,270 --> 00:15:47,659
s-stop making things worse.

224
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:48,940
Just come home,
apologize to Dad,

225
00:15:49,050 --> 00:15:49,580
and back down a bit...

226
00:15:49,581 --> 00:15:51,240
Then everything will be fine.

227
00:16:04,750 --> 00:16:07,080
Where would you get all that money, Yun Li?

228
00:16:14,530 --> 00:16:16,290
Why did I have to act so tough?

229
00:17:00,390 --> 00:17:01,390
Shize.

230
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:04,540
Why did I have to cross paths with you?

231
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:11,880
Yuan...

232
00:18:03,900 --> 00:18:05,829
The money has been transferred to you.

233
00:18:05,830 --> 00:18:06,830
Cut the crap.

234
00:18:58,500 --> 00:18:59,500
Hello?
Ms. Idle Cloud.

235
00:19:00,110 --> 00:19:01,179
We'll all gather

236
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:01,850
in the lobby of the Experience Center

237
00:19:01,851 --> 00:19:03,310
at 3 p.m. this afternoon.

238
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:04,250
The company has arranged

239
00:19:04,251 --> 00:19:06,109
a visit and hands-on
experience session for everyone.

240
00:19:06,110 --> 00:19:07,749
Please be sure to attend on time.

241
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:08,750
Okay, I will.

242
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:13,160
3 p.m.

243
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:28,249
What you are seeing now

244
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:29,250
is our...

245
00:19:29,290 --> 00:19:31,179
I'll watch whatever
video Mr. Feishui makes.

246
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:32,180
This is the first floor

247
00:19:32,181 --> 00:19:33,780
of our VR experience center.

248
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:36,960
You are...

249
00:19:37,410 --> 00:19:39,330
I'm Idle Cloud Tick-Tock.

250
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:41,220
Oh, Ms. Idle Cloud!

251
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:42,960
We chatted through private messages

252
00:19:42,961 --> 00:19:44,159
on EAW before.

253
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:45,219
I'm Fairy Feifei,

254
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:46,679
a dance-section content creator.

255
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,000
Oh yeah, we did.
Let me introduce.

256
00:19:48,850 --> 00:19:49,850
Mr. Feishui.

257
00:19:50,350 --> 00:19:51,979
He's one of the top 10

258
00:19:51,980 --> 00:19:52,980
most influential content creators on EAW.

259
00:19:52,981 --> 00:19:54,239
Hello.

260
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:56,089
And there's Ms. Can't-Know-It-All.

261
00:19:56,090 --> 00:19:57,090
Hello.

262
00:19:57,770 --> 00:19:58,979
Hello, Ms. Idle Cloud.

263
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:00,809
We just got the phone set up

264
00:20:00,810 --> 00:20:01,959
and are about to do a test recording.

265
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:02,960
Awesome.
See you in a bit.

266
00:20:05,050 --> 00:20:06,659
Are you a bit shy around people?

267
00:20:06,660 --> 00:20:07,480
It's okay.

268
00:20:07,510 --> 00:20:08,659
Everyone here's really nice.

269
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:09,660
Don't be afraid.

270
00:20:11,610 --> 00:20:12,690
Mr. K.
Isn't this the latest

271
00:20:13,070 --> 00:20:13,960
drone model?

272
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:15,509
You got your hands on it so fast.

273
00:20:15,510 --> 00:20:16,790
As
Professional content creators,

274
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:18,609
we must deliver

275
00:20:18,610 --> 00:20:19,310
the best visual effects

276
00:20:19,311 --> 00:20:20,459
to our fans.

277
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:21,460
The best.

278
00:20:22,110 --> 00:20:23,110
Mr. K.

279
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:25,980
This drone is so cool.

280
00:20:26,180 --> 00:20:27,380
It must be expensive.

281
00:20:27,770 --> 00:20:28,770
It's the Magic 3.

282
00:20:29,050 --> 00:20:30,050
Not only is it expensive,

283
00:20:30,051 --> 00:20:31,510
it's also very hard to get.

284
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,309
My friend's company developed it.

285
00:20:33,310 --> 00:20:34,250
If you guys want one,

286
00:20:34,251 --> 00:20:35,650
just let me know anytime.

287
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:37,009
But it's so high-end.

288
00:20:37,010 --> 00:20:38,349
Is it hard to fly?

289
00:20:38,350 --> 00:20:39,350
It's easy.

290
00:20:39,550 --> 00:20:41,050
A quadcopter like this

291
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:42,309
is basically like a remote-control car.

292
00:20:42,310 --> 00:20:43,220
Anyone can fly it.

293
00:20:43,221 --> 00:20:44,750
This is an octocopter.

294
00:20:47,610 --> 00:20:49,249
Although it only has 4 arms,

295
00:20:49,250 --> 00:20:50,070
each arm has

296
00:20:50,090 --> 00:20:51,749
2 motors and 2 propellers, one
on top and one on the bottom,

297
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,410
which makes it an octocopter.

298
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:57,419
Its special carbon fiber alloy propellers

299
00:20:57,420 --> 00:20:58,050
allow it

300
00:20:58,051 --> 00:21:00,009
to operate normally across
a wide temperature range.

301
00:21:00,010 --> 00:21:01,069
It features a 100-megapixel

302
00:21:01,070 --> 00:21:02,459
Hasselblad main camera,

303
00:21:02,460 --> 00:21:04,720
omnidirectional intelligent tracking

304
00:21:04,810 --> 00:21:05,810
and vision sensing,

305
00:21:05,811 --> 00:21:07,569
low-light active obstacle avoidance,

306
00:21:07,570 --> 00:21:08,749
and a 360-degree rotating gimbal.

307
00:21:08,750 --> 00:21:10,150
It's really impressive.

308
00:21:12,350 --> 00:21:14,659
Ah... I know this.

309
00:21:14,660 --> 00:21:15,010
I...

310
00:21:15,011 --> 00:21:16,210
Of course I know this.

311
00:21:17,010 --> 00:21:18,740
It was just a slip of the tongue.

312
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:21,160
Wait, who are you?

313
00:21:22,380 --> 00:21:22,920
I'm

314
00:21:22,921 --> 00:21:24,659
a tech-section content creator,

315
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:25,920
Idle Cloud Tick-Tock.

316
00:21:26,750 --> 00:21:27,920
Idle Cloud what?

317
00:21:28,750 --> 00:21:30,150
Idle Cloud Tick-Tock...

318
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,160
Hello, everyone.

319
00:21:32,180 --> 00:21:33,180
Welcome to

320
00:21:33,181 --> 00:21:34,549
the EAW Experience Hall.

321
00:21:34,550 --> 00:21:35,679
I'm your guide,

322
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:36,680
He Jiameng.

323
00:21:36,770 --> 00:21:37,899
EAW

324
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:39,179
is the first

325
00:21:39,180 --> 00:21:40,849
virtual reality experience hall in Nanwu.

326
00:21:40,850 --> 00:21:42,050
Its full name is Enjoy Another

327
00:21:42,330 --> 00:21:43,330
World.

328
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:44,509
This is also our company's

329
00:21:44,510 --> 00:21:45,549
core philosophy.

330
00:21:45,550 --> 00:21:47,049
At the moment, our main projects

331
00:21:47,050 --> 00:21:49,220
include VR device development,

332
00:21:49,380 --> 00:21:50,699
VR gaming experiences,

333
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:51,200
smart

334
00:21:51,201 --> 00:21:53,159
living scenario simulations, and more.

335
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:54,050
The exhibition hall

336
00:21:54,051 --> 00:21:55,110
we're in now

337
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:57,360
is our Smart Living Experience Center.

338
00:21:57,980 --> 00:21:59,009
Feel free

339
00:21:59,010 --> 00:22:00,159
to explore on your own,

340
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:00,960
and if you need anything

341
00:22:00,961 --> 00:22:02,360
just let me know anytime.

342
00:22:02,660 --> 00:22:04,379
We have many types here.

343
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:05,399
If you are interested,

344
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:07,200
you can experience it yourself.

345
00:22:08,460 --> 00:22:09,460
Hello, Tangy.

346
00:22:10,050 --> 00:22:11,050
I'm right...

347
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:13,659
Everyone, take a look here as well.

348
00:22:13,660 --> 00:22:15,590
The equipment is really advanced.

349
00:22:18,010 --> 00:22:19,070
You mean the face?

350
00:22:20,550 --> 00:22:22,350
The entire body from head to toe.

351
00:22:22,420 --> 00:22:23,420
Miss He.

352
00:22:24,110 --> 00:22:24,660
Um,

353
00:22:24,661 --> 00:22:26,089
is there a place to charge here?

354
00:22:26,090 --> 00:22:27,440
My phone is dead.

355
00:22:27,940 --> 00:22:29,670
You can charge it in the lounge.

356
00:22:30,030 --> 00:22:30,530
Okay.

357
00:22:30,531 --> 00:22:31,549
Do you want me to take you there?

358
00:22:31,550 --> 00:22:33,369
No need, I can go by myself. Thanks.

359
00:22:33,370 --> 00:22:34,479
This is the project.

360
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:36,340
You can go over and experience it.

361
00:22:55,660 --> 00:22:56,660
Hello, Tangy.

362
00:22:57,050 --> 00:22:58,179
What's going on with you?

363
00:22:58,180 --> 00:23:00,049
Why couldn't I get through to your phone?

364
00:23:00,050 --> 00:23:01,309
My phone died.

365
00:23:01,310 --> 00:23:02,959
I just plugged it in to charge.

366
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:04,380
I was so worried.

367
00:23:04,460 --> 00:23:06,520
I thought something happened to you.

368
00:23:07,220 --> 00:23:08,310
Where are you now?

369
00:23:08,880 --> 00:23:09,960
I'm visiting EAW right now.

370
00:23:10,980 --> 00:23:11,980
EAW?

371
00:23:13,270 --> 00:23:14,609
A relative of my college roommate

372
00:23:14,610 --> 00:23:15,719
works at EAW.

373
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:17,069
Do you want me to introduce you

374
00:23:17,070 --> 00:23:18,600
so they can look out for you?

375
00:23:18,610 --> 00:23:19,420
N-No need.

376
00:23:19,570 --> 00:23:20,809
Don't go to the trouble.

377
00:23:20,810 --> 00:23:21,810
It's no trouble.

378
00:23:22,050 --> 00:23:22,810
Her name is Xia.

379
00:23:22,811 --> 00:23:23,870
She's really nice.

380
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:25,959
T-There's really no need for that, Tangy.

381
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:26,680
I bet you're just

382
00:23:26,681 --> 00:23:28,610
scared of talking to older people.

383
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:31,750
You really know me.

384
00:23:31,980 --> 00:23:33,419
With the way you are,

385
00:23:33,420 --> 00:23:36,020
how can you manage to
live on your own out there?

386
00:23:36,250 --> 00:23:37,349
You didn't secretly cry

387
00:23:37,350 --> 00:23:39,150
at the hotel last night, did you?

388
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:40,979
I didn't cry,

389
00:23:40,980 --> 00:23:42,770
but I was scared out of my wits.

390
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:44,980
What happened?

391
00:23:45,380 --> 00:23:46,509
Let me tell you. The driver

392
00:23:46,510 --> 00:23:47,569
who picked me up last night

393
00:23:47,570 --> 00:23:48,550
was terrifying.

394
00:23:48,551 --> 00:23:49,609
He had this cold expression the whole ride

395
00:23:49,610 --> 00:23:51,069
and didn't say a single word.

396
00:23:51,070 --> 00:23:52,419
And the roads were pitch black.

397
00:23:52,420 --> 00:23:53,569
I was so nervous

398
00:23:53,570 --> 00:23:55,430
I even had nightmares afterward.

399
00:23:55,610 --> 00:23:56,940
What kind of nightmare?

400
00:23:57,900 --> 00:24:00,679
I dreamed he stabbed me to death

401
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:02,180
with my umbrella.

402
00:24:03,030 --> 00:24:05,030
How could an umbrella kill someone?

403
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:07,589
Maybe it was just because
of the atmosphere last night.

404
00:24:07,590 --> 00:24:08,639
It was raining,

405
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:10,069
and the whole situation felt like
something out of a suspense movie.

406
00:24:10,070 --> 00:24:11,570
And I lent him my umbrella.

407
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:13,380
That dream's way too ominous.

408
00:24:13,530 --> 00:24:14,480
The umbrella you lent him

409
00:24:14,481 --> 00:24:16,080
turned into a deadly weapon.

410
00:24:16,290 --> 00:24:17,899
You'd better get the umbrella
back as soon as possible.

411
00:24:17,900 --> 00:24:19,379
I wouldn't feel comfortable
knowing the "murder weapon"

412
00:24:19,380 --> 00:24:21,029
is still with the "murderer."

413
00:24:21,030 --> 00:24:22,740
L-Listen to me carefully.

414
00:24:23,270 --> 00:24:24,380
I have a feeling

415
00:24:24,790 --> 00:24:26,650
that he looks somewhat familiar.

416
00:24:34,590 --> 00:24:35,400
Tangy.

417
00:24:35,420 --> 00:24:36,499
I feel like there's someone

418
00:24:36,500 --> 00:24:37,500
in my room.

419
00:24:37,820 --> 00:24:39,360
H-Hold on a second.

420
00:25:01,110 --> 00:25:01,920
I'm sorry.

421
00:25:01,921 --> 00:25:04,520
I-I didn't know there
was someone in this room.

422
00:26:00,490 --> 00:26:01,490
Your umbrella.

423
00:26:16,050 --> 00:26:17,050
Thanks.

424
00:26:18,540 --> 00:26:19,540
You're welcome.

425
00:26:33,570 --> 00:26:34,630
A folding umbrella

426
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:37,120
can't possibly kill anyone.

427
00:26:40,450 --> 00:26:42,180
A straight-handled one might.

428
00:26:44,820 --> 00:26:47,080
Then what kind of umbrella could kill...

429
00:26:49,210 --> 00:26:51,210
I mean, what kind of umbrella

430
00:26:51,230 --> 00:26:52,490
should I avoid buying?

431
00:26:52,940 --> 00:26:54,740
You don't have enough strength.

432
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:57,040
It wouldn't matter what you buy.

433
00:26:59,720 --> 00:27:00,880
I see. I...

434
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:02,880
Thanks for the advice.

435
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:25,810
Ms. Idle Cloud, wanna
take a photo together?

436
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:28,249
How many followers does she have

437
00:27:28,250 --> 00:27:29,669
to be acting so full of herself?

438
00:27:29,670 --> 00:27:31,520
M-Maybe it's just too noisy

439
00:27:31,550 --> 00:27:32,810
and she didn't hear us.

440
00:27:34,380 --> 00:27:35,380
Ms. Idle Cloud.

441
00:27:35,850 --> 00:27:37,050
Are you free tonight?

442
00:27:37,880 --> 00:27:38,720
What's up?

443
00:27:38,820 --> 00:27:39,760
You weren't here just now.

444
00:27:39,761 --> 00:27:41,049
I've notified everyone else

445
00:27:41,050 --> 00:27:42,679
that Mr. Xu wanted to invite

446
00:27:42,680 --> 00:27:44,849
all the content creators
for a get-together tonight.

447
00:27:44,850 --> 00:27:46,659
So we're having dinner together?

448
00:27:46,660 --> 00:27:47,850
It's not mandatory.

449
00:27:48,050 --> 00:27:49,980
If you don't want to go,

450
00:27:50,090 --> 00:27:51,739
I'll tell him you have other plans.

451
00:27:51,740 --> 00:27:53,720
Okay. Thank you, Miss He.

452
00:27:54,750 --> 00:27:56,109
How was your tour just now?

453
00:27:56,110 --> 00:27:57,210
Is everyone here?

454
00:27:57,530 --> 00:27:58,530
Yes.

455
00:27:59,350 --> 00:28:00,610
This is Ms. Idle Cloud.

456
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:02,110
This is our boss, Mr. Xu.

457
00:28:02,270 --> 00:28:03,270
Hello.

458
00:28:03,510 --> 00:28:04,510
Hello.

459
00:28:05,010 --> 00:28:06,010
I'm Xu Qingsong.

460
00:28:06,500 --> 00:28:07,550
Hello, Mr. Xu.

461
00:28:08,740 --> 00:28:10,009
Thank you all for taking the
time out of your busy schedules

462
00:28:10,010 --> 00:28:11,010
to participate.

463
00:28:11,290 --> 00:28:12,180
I'm the owner of EAW,

464
00:28:12,181 --> 00:28:13,330
Xu Qingsong.

465
00:28:13,850 --> 00:28:15,300
Please forgive us

466
00:28:15,380 --> 00:28:17,220
if our hospitality falls short.

467
00:28:17,980 --> 00:28:19,340
We'd appreciate your help
in making

468
00:28:19,920 --> 00:28:21,720
EAW's promotional videos then.

469
00:28:22,090 --> 00:28:23,530
Thank you, Mr. Xu.

470
00:28:23,810 --> 00:28:25,410
Thank you for your hard work.

471
00:28:27,140 --> 00:28:28,140
Mr. Xu.

472
00:28:29,090 --> 00:28:29,900
I didn't expect

473
00:28:29,901 --> 00:28:31,630
you to be so young and handsome.

474
00:28:32,490 --> 00:28:33,290
You are?

475
00:28:33,380 --> 00:28:34,640
Just call me Feifei.

476
00:28:35,420 --> 00:28:36,570
Hello, Ms. Feifei.

477
00:28:36,930 --> 00:28:39,219
Thank you for coming to
help with the promotion.

478
00:28:39,220 --> 00:28:41,160
No need to address me with "Ms."

479
00:28:41,570 --> 00:28:42,830
It makes me sound old.

480
00:28:43,410 --> 00:28:45,040
Can I just call you Qingsong?

481
00:28:47,350 --> 00:28:48,569
Let's add each other on WeChat, shall we?

482
00:28:48,570 --> 00:28:49,879
That way, after I finish editing the video,

483
00:28:49,880 --> 00:28:51,010
I can send it to you,

484
00:28:51,050 --> 00:28:52,910
and you can give me some guidance.

485
00:28:52,980 --> 00:28:54,510
I won't call it "guidance."

486
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:56,459
Just do it as you normally would.

487
00:28:56,460 --> 00:28:57,180
And when the video is ready,

488
00:28:57,181 --> 00:28:59,040
just send it directly to Jiameng.

489
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:00,480
Thank you.

490
00:29:04,850 --> 00:29:06,720
Are all bosses this cool?

491
00:29:11,660 --> 00:29:13,480
Welcome to

492
00:29:13,550 --> 00:29:14,550
Wings of the Sky.

493
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:17,030
Here, you'll become a pilot,

494
00:29:17,070 --> 00:29:18,419
and we'll take you on

495
00:29:18,420 --> 00:29:20,330
an immersive flying experience.

496
00:29:20,430 --> 00:29:21,430
Young lady,

497
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:23,010
you want to try this?

498
00:29:23,530 --> 00:29:24,530
Yes.

499
00:29:24,650 --> 00:29:25,500
Good taste.

500
00:29:25,530 --> 00:29:26,769
Do you want me to take you there?

501
00:29:26,770 --> 00:29:27,090
No need.

502
00:29:27,091 --> 00:29:28,400
I can go by myself.

503
00:29:29,640 --> 00:29:30,940
[Xia]

504
00:29:34,180 --> 00:29:35,290
That old man

505
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:37,440
must be Xia's relative.

506
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Ms. Idle Cloud.

507
00:29:47,850 --> 00:29:48,850
Mr. Xu.

508
00:29:50,070 --> 00:29:51,070
You want to try this?
Yes.

509
00:29:52,830 --> 00:29:54,030
Great taste.
This game features

510
00:29:54,500 --> 00:29:56,639
cutting-edge spatial awareness technology,

511
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:58,100
but it can be a bit intense.

512
00:29:58,350 --> 00:29:59,480
Do you want to try it?

513
00:30:00,590 --> 00:30:01,440
And I'll highlight this

514
00:30:01,441 --> 00:30:02,830
in my video.

515
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:04,340
That's great.

516
00:30:04,570 --> 00:30:06,226
Wait a moment,
I'll get someone here for you.

517
00:30:06,250 --> 00:30:07,250
Okay.

518
00:30:07,770 --> 00:30:09,570
Let me show you around the front.

519
00:30:11,730 --> 00:30:12,790
Help out with this.

520
00:30:18,110 --> 00:30:20,020
We're short-handed.

521
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:21,520
Thanks.

522
00:30:22,790 --> 00:30:24,590
Don't keep her waiting too long.

523
00:30:26,640 --> 00:30:27,900
He'll help you with it.

524
00:30:28,710 --> 00:30:30,270
Why is it him again?

525
00:30:48,630 --> 00:30:50,360
Put your feet into these rings.

526
00:31:05,880 --> 00:31:06,880
Is it too tight?

527
00:31:08,550 --> 00:31:09,550
No.

528
00:31:09,830 --> 00:31:11,190
Impressive.
You handle it with ease

529
00:31:11,610 --> 00:31:12,940
on your first try.

530
00:31:15,350 --> 00:31:16,350
Ms. Idle Cloud,

531
00:31:16,930 --> 00:31:18,190
enjoy the experience.

532
00:31:23,380 --> 00:31:26,040
Have you never tied this
for anyone else before?

533
00:31:28,460 --> 00:31:29,460
No.

534
00:31:30,090 --> 00:31:32,460
Then have you attended any training?

535
00:31:32,810 --> 00:31:33,810
What training?

536
00:31:34,810 --> 00:31:37,999
Like how to tie this safety rope

537
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:38,850
most securely

538
00:31:38,851 --> 00:31:40,609
and minimize

539
00:31:40,610 --> 00:31:41,700
the risk factor.

540
00:31:42,180 --> 00:31:43,180
No.

541
00:31:46,460 --> 00:31:47,050
Then,

542
00:31:47,200 --> 00:31:48,699
if it's not fastened properly,

543
00:31:48,700 --> 00:31:50,110
could I get thrown out?

544
00:31:53,700 --> 00:31:54,700
No idea.

545
00:32:08,500 --> 00:32:10,700
Don't worry, I've checked everything.

546
00:32:16,740 --> 00:32:18,030
The game has started.

547
00:32:18,180 --> 00:32:19,570
Please get ready.

548
00:33:25,640 --> 00:33:26,880
So cute.

549
00:33:57,910 --> 00:33:59,560
The game is about to end.

550
00:34:14,389 --> 00:34:15,620
S-Sorry.

551
00:34:15,940 --> 00:34:17,479
T-The experience was too real.

552
00:34:17,480 --> 00:34:19,510
I felt weightless all of a sudden.

553
00:34:24,050 --> 00:34:25,130
I want to ask,

554
00:34:26,100 --> 00:34:27,409
is this game

555
00:34:27,429 --> 00:34:28,929
supposed to have no sound?

556
00:34:30,340 --> 00:34:31,399
I-I just noticed

557
00:34:31,400 --> 00:34:32,360
the NPC was speaking,

558
00:34:32,361 --> 00:34:33,889
but I didn't hear any sound.

559
00:34:39,360 --> 00:34:40,900
The game's over.

560
00:34:41,030 --> 00:34:43,360
Welcome to experience it again next time.

561
00:34:48,300 --> 00:34:49,300
It has sound,

562
00:34:49,730 --> 00:34:52,440
but the right ear
channel seems to be broken.

563
00:34:56,170 --> 00:34:57,170
Did you

564
00:34:57,550 --> 00:34:59,150
hear nothing at all just now?

565
00:35:00,170 --> 00:35:01,170
Yeah.

566
00:35:01,440 --> 00:35:03,050
Maybe I was just too nervous

567
00:35:03,300 --> 00:35:04,360
and didn't hear it.

568
00:35:10,780 --> 00:35:12,230
I hope he didn't realize

569
00:35:12,420 --> 00:35:14,300
that my left ear is deaf.

570
00:35:18,820 --> 00:35:20,050
Impressive, Mr. K.

571
00:35:23,940 --> 00:35:24,670
Mr. K,

572
00:35:24,940 --> 00:35:26,170
you're so amazing.

573
00:35:27,610 --> 00:35:28,610
This is nothing.

574
00:35:28,730 --> 00:35:30,730
I'll do an even better trick for you.

575
00:35:37,610 --> 00:35:39,030
C-Crap.

576
00:35:41,150 --> 00:35:42,150
Crap. Crap.

577
00:35:43,400 --> 00:35:44,729
I-I-I borrowed this.

578
00:35:44,730 --> 00:35:46,050
What should I do?

579
00:35:50,210 --> 00:35:51,210
Need help?

580
00:36:03,710 --> 00:36:04,710
Let me try.

581
00:36:36,580 --> 00:36:38,440
How many times did he make it spin?

582
00:36:45,960 --> 00:36:47,620
It can actually fly like this?

583
00:37:14,730 --> 00:37:15,780
Cube Roll!

584
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:16,920
Unique's

585
00:37:16,921 --> 00:37:17,979
youngest member,

586
00:37:17,980 --> 00:37:18,760
Fu Shize,

587
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:20,940
is now executing the Cube Roll!

588
00:38:06,340 --> 00:38:07,340
It should be fine now.

589
00:38:07,400 --> 00:38:08,400
Give it a try.

590
00:38:08,760 --> 00:38:09,760
Thank you.

591
00:38:18,800 --> 00:38:19,800
Handsome,

592
00:38:20,590 --> 00:38:22,090
can I add you on...

593
00:38:27,560 --> 00:38:29,310
It's him.

594
00:38:54,030 --> 00:38:56,000
Given the surface area of a cone,

595
00:38:56,150 --> 00:38:57,589
and knowing that its lateral surface

596
00:38:57,590 --> 00:38:58,480
is a semicircle,

597
00:38:58,481 --> 00:39:00,279
what is its volume?

598
00:39:00,280 --> 00:39:00,880
We've talked about

599
00:39:00,881 --> 00:39:02,440
this math problem before.

600
00:39:03,070 --> 00:39:04,280
Who can answer it?

601
00:39:06,480 --> 00:39:07,480
Yun Li.

602
00:39:08,150 --> 00:39:09,150
You answer it.

603
00:39:10,250 --> 00:39:11,250
Yun Li?

604
00:39:16,180 --> 00:39:17,240
What did I just ask?

605
00:39:19,710 --> 00:39:20,840
I'm sorry, Teacher.

606
00:39:20,880 --> 00:39:22,010
I didn't catch that.

607
00:39:25,170 --> 00:39:26,170
Yun Li,

608
00:39:26,260 --> 00:39:27,940
you need to focus in class.

609
00:39:28,680 --> 00:39:29,810
Go stand in the back.

610
00:39:33,710 --> 00:39:34,710
Quiet.

611
00:39:35,720 --> 00:39:37,650
Let's move to the second question.

612
00:39:42,780 --> 00:39:44,469
How could it be? You must be kidding.

613
00:39:44,470 --> 00:39:46,390
That's her.

614
00:39:48,150 --> 00:39:48,710
Over here!

615
00:39:48,711 --> 00:39:49,960
I heard she's deaf.

616
00:39:50,130 --> 00:39:51,419
She's probably faking it.

617
00:39:51,420 --> 00:39:52,420
Who knows.

618
00:39:55,550 --> 00:39:57,010
Watch where you're going.

619
00:39:57,190 --> 00:39:58,589
Is that the girl from your class?

620
00:39:58,590 --> 00:39:59,590
Yeah, that's her.

621
00:40:14,340 --> 00:40:16,140
The drone operation is amazing!

622
00:40:16,150 --> 00:40:18,109
Mr. Streamer, your
drone skills are god-tier!

623
00:40:18,110 --> 00:40:19,770
Waiting for a drone tutorial.

624
00:40:19,820 --> 00:40:21,549
Near XUST Library.

625
00:40:21,550 --> 00:40:22,780
Looks so familiar.

626
00:40:22,820 --> 00:40:24,530
XUST alumni, come together!

627
00:40:28,230 --> 00:40:30,210
In my bleak school days,

628
00:40:30,630 --> 00:40:32,800
he was one of the few rays of light.

629
00:40:33,780 --> 00:40:35,800
Unlike the scorching sun,

630
00:40:36,650 --> 00:40:38,980
his presence was

631
00:40:39,480 --> 00:40:41,410
as gentle and bright as moonlight.

632
00:40:51,580 --> 00:40:53,090
[National College Drone Competition]

633
00:41:29,480 --> 00:41:30,030
Unique's

634
00:41:30,031 --> 00:41:31,149
youngest member,

635
00:41:31,150 --> 00:41:32,000
Fu Shize,

636
00:41:32,070 --> 00:41:34,069
is now executing the Cube Roll

637
00:41:34,070 --> 00:41:35,109
to overtake the other team!

638
00:41:35,110 --> 00:41:35,940
Unique is now

639
00:41:35,941 --> 00:41:37,200
taking the lead again!

640
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:46,920
Bravo!

641
00:41:47,030 --> 00:41:47,800
Friends,

642
00:41:47,801 --> 00:41:50,509
what a thrilling match!

643
00:41:50,510 --> 00:41:51,799
Congratulations to Unique

644
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:53,759
for winning the national championship!

645
00:41:53,760 --> 00:41:55,319
And congratulations to Fu Shize,

646
00:41:55,320 --> 00:41:57,229
the youngest

647
00:41:57,230 --> 00:41:58,319
genius of XUST,

648
00:41:58,320 --> 00:41:59,709
for setting a new record!

649
00:41:59,710 --> 00:42:01,000
This is incredible!

650
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:08,879
Champion! Champion! Champion!

651
00:42:08,880 --> 00:42:11,800
At that moment, he was
the center of attention,

652
00:42:12,320 --> 00:42:14,669
radiating a spirit that
nothing in this world

653
00:42:14,670 --> 00:42:15,670
could defeat.

654
00:42:30,760 --> 00:42:31,980
It's been 7 years.

655
00:42:33,130 --> 00:42:35,130
I finally get to see you again.

656
00:42:42,680 --> 00:42:43,680
Ms. Idle Cloud.

657
00:42:44,160 --> 00:42:45,330
Here you are.

658
00:42:45,500 --> 00:42:46,960
I've been looking for you.

659
00:42:47,150 --> 00:42:48,759
I want to confirm with you again.

660
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:49,819
Are you really not going

661
00:42:49,820 --> 00:42:51,080
to the dinner tonight?

662
00:42:51,260 --> 00:42:52,260
I am going.

